# meta-rini

Custom Yocto Project meta-layer for embedded Linux development.
Built and tested on Raspberry Pi 4 (64-bit) using Yocto Scarthgap (LTS).

## Layer Contents

| Recipe         |              Description                      |
|----------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| system-monitor | Shell script service with systemd integration |
| hello-embedded | C program demonstrating cross-compilation |
| legacy-app | Migration example — Kirkstone to Scarthgap syntax |

## Compatibility

| Yocto Release | Status |
|---------------|--------|
| Scarthgap (5.0 LTS) | ✓ Tested |
| Kirkstone (4.0 LTS) | Migration reference only |

## Hardware Tested

- Raspberry Pi 4 (raspberrypi4-64 machine config)
- BeagleBone Black (am335x BSP — Week 2)

## Key Learnings Demonstrated

- Custom layer creation with layer.conf and LAYERSERIES_COMPAT
- Recipe writing with do_compile, do_install, inherit autotools
- bbappend for non-invasive upstream recipe modification
- Kirkstone → Scarthgap migration (colon override syntax)
- sstate-cache configuration for optimized builds
- devtool modify/finish workflow for patch creation
- systemd service integration via inherit systemd

## Build Setup

\`\`\`bash
# Clone alongside poky:
git clone -b scarthgap git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky.git
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/meta-rini.git

# Initialize build:
source poky/oe-init-build-env build-rpi

# Add layer:
bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rini

# Build:
MACHINE=raspberrypi4-64 bitbake core-image-minimal
\`\`\`
